# Cisco EIGRP Dynamic Routing Lab

## Project Overview

This project demonstrates the implementation of EIGRP (Enhanced Interior Gateway Routing Protocol) in a multi-router enterprise network using Cisco Packet Tracer. The network was designed to establish dynamic routing between interconnected networks and enable automatic route learning across the infrastructure.

The lab simulates a real-world enterprise routing environment where routers exchange routing information to provide end-to-end connectivity between hosts located on different networks.

---

## Technologies and Concepts Used

- Cisco Packet Tracer
- EIGRP Dynamic Routing
- Automatic Route Learning
- Multi-Router Connectivity
- IP Addressing and Subnetting
- Cisco IOS CLI
- Enterprise Routing Concepts
- Network Verification and Troubleshooting

---

## Network Topology

The topology consists of:

- 5 Cisco 2811 Routers
- 2 Cisco 2960 Switches
- Multiple End Devices (PCs)
- Multiple interconnected routed networks

### Configured Networks

- 192.168.1.0/24
- 192.168.2.0/24
- 192.168.12.0/24
- 192.168.23.0/24
- 192.168.34.0/24
- 192.168.45.0/24

---

## Network Features

### EIGRP Dynamic Routing
Configured EIGRP routing between routers to dynamically advertise and learn remote network routes.

### Automatic Route Learning
Enabled routers to automatically exchange routing information and update routing tables dynamically.

### Neighbor Relationship Formation
Established EIGRP neighbor adjacencies between directly connected routers.

### Router Interface Configuration
Assigned IP addresses to router interfaces according to the provided topology.

### End-to-End Connectivity
Established successful communication between hosts located on different routed networks.

---

## Verification and Testing

The following verifications were successfully completed:

- EIGRP configuration verification
- Neighbor relationship verification
- Dynamic route learning verification
- Router interface verification
- Routing table analysis
- Successful end-to-end connectivity testing

---

## Verification Commands Used

```bash
show running-config
show ip route
show ip eigrp neighbors
show ip protocols
show ip interface brief
ping [destination-ip]
```

